      "tree_id": "95a3646b70b8fc6ac191ea3ea75a6af598637d57",
      "message": "DFT submission: saving 30201659/10000000000 (#90)\n\nAdd submissions/dft/zeph1912-rank-moment-refinement, a numerical\nrefinement of the rate certificate in HalitZiyaKARTAL's #41\n(submissions/dft/halitziyakartal-halitziyav4-logception).\n\nThe P16A8Z circuit, its rank multisets, the strict tensor engine,\nSussman's mixed-target recursion and the Fourier reduction are unchanged.\nTighter rational enclosures of the rank moments (sixth/fifth-order\nexponential bounds with finite-series logarithm certificates) and a\ntensor power of 11640 instead of 7760 certify the rate\nC = 60403319/20000000000 (0.00302016595), above the C0 = 4719/1562500\ncertified in #41. Race.bound is proved at the saving 30201659/10000000000\n(about 0.0030201659) through the seam saving 3020165925/10^12.\n\nFiles: 411 of the 462 Lean files are byte-identical to #41; 3 OpenAI\nmodel files change only their Mathlib import; 15 are modified and 33\nare new. Source credits are kept in the file headers.\n\nArtifact:\nhttps://github.com/zeph1912/Discrete-Fourier-Transform-Refinement-2026_10_31\n(commit 8cd46642a51103b1462051c75102b4089340dff2),\nZenodo DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23843356.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
